        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14838\">PR #14838</a> from <code>jrandolf:bindgen-map-param-ref</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For an exported function taking an anonymous <code>map&lt;K, V&gt;</code>, <code>bindgen!</code> generated a by-value <code>HashMap</code> of borrowed keys and values (e.g. <code>HashMap&lt;&amp;str, &amp;[String]&gt;</code>), so callers holding a <code>HashMap&lt;String, Vec&lt;String&gt;&gt;</code> had to build a second map of references to make a call. This mirrors how lists are handled instead: in borrowed positions the map is taken by reference, and with <code>Ownership::Owning</code> its keys and values are owned. Named map types already generated <code>&amp;Named</code>.</p>\n<p>This changes generated signatures, see #14831. It's based on #14834; only the last commit is new.</p>\n<p>Closes #14831<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
